@ghostId = 64b7f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0

### 0. Logout first, so there is no cookie
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/logout

### U1. Me without a token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me

### U2. Me with a fake token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi

### U3. Me as Sara -> 200, user without password
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### U4. All users as Sara (normal user) -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### U5. All users as admin -> 200 with the list and a count
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### U6. All users with no token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users





### U7. Sara reads her own id -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### U8. Sara reads the admin's id -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{adminId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### U9. Admin reads Sara -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### U10. Admin, an id that does not exist -> 404 "User not found"
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{ghostId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### U11. Admin, a broken id -> 400 "Invalid value for _id"
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### U12. No token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}

### U13. Sara, an id that does not exist -> 403 (the same answer as U8)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{ghostId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### U14. Sara, a broken id -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}




### U15. Name only -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sara Hassan" }

### U16. Email with capitals and spaces -> 200, saved as lowercase without spaces
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "  SARA.New@Example.com " }

### U17. Both fields, back to the original email -> 200 (run right after U16)
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sara Ali", "email": "sara@example.com" }

### U18. Nothing to change -> 400 "Please provide name or email"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### U19. Name is an object -> 400 "name must be text"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": { "$gt": "" } }

### U20. Empty name -> 400 "Please provide name"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "" }

### U21. Short name -> 400 "Name must be at least 3 characters"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "ab" }

### U22. Bad email -> 400 "Please provide a valid email"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nope" }

### U23. Email already used by the admin -> 409 "Duplicate value entered for email..."
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@example.com" }

### U23b. Admin's email with capitals and spaces -> 409 (the clean value is checked)
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "  ADMIN@Example.COM " }

### U24. Sneaking in role and password -> 200, but both are ignored
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sara Ali", "role": "admin", "password": "hacked123" }

### U25. No token -> 401
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sara Ali" }




### U26. No token -> 401
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me/password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "oldPassword": "secret123", "newPassword": "newpass456" }

### U27. Empty body -> 400 "Please provide oldPassword and newPassword"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### U28. newPassword is an object -> 400, same message
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "oldPassword": "secret123", "newPassword": { "$gt": "" } }

### U29. Wrong old password -> 400 "Old password is incorrect"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "oldPassword": "wrong-one", "newPassword": "newpass456" }

### U30. Same password -> 400 "New password must be different from the old password"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "oldPassword": "secret123", "newPassword": "secret123" }

### U31. New password too short -> 400 "Password must be at least 6 characters"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "oldPassword": "secret123", "newPassword": "abc" }

### U32. Success -> 200 {msg, accessToken}; also sets a new refresh cookie
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "oldPassword": "secret123", "newPassword": "newpass456" }

> {%
  client.global.set('userToken', response.body.accessToken)
%}

### U33. The OLD login (from login B) is dead -> 401
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Cookie: refreshToken={{firstRefresh}}

### U34. This device's NEW cookie works on /auth/refresh -> 200 (the important check)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh

> {%
  client.global.set('userToken', response.body.accessToken)
%}

### U35. Login with the OLD password -> 401
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "sara@example.com", "password": "secret123" }

### U36. Login with the NEW password -> 200
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "sara@example.com", "password": "newpass456" }

> {%
  client.global.set('userToken', response.body.accessToken)
%}

### U37. Change it back so the other tests keep working -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "oldPassword": "newpass456", "newPassword": "secret123" }

> {%
  client.global.set('userToken', response.body.accessToken)
%}






### U38. No token -> 401
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}/role
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "manager" }

### U39. Sara (user) tries -> 403 "You are not allowed to access this route"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "manager" }

### U40. Admin, unknown role -> 400 "Role must be one of: user, manager, admin"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "superuser" }

### U41. Role is an object -> 400, same message
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": { "$gt": "" } }

### U42. No role -> 400, same message
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### U43. Admin changes their own role -> 403 "You cannot change your own role"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{adminId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "user" }

### U44. Id that does not exist -> 404 "User not found"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{ghostId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "manager" }

### U45. Broken id -> 400 "Invalid value for _id"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/abc/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "manager" }

### U46. Admin makes Sara a manager -> 200, role "manager", name NOT changed
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "manager", "name": "Hacker" }

### U47. Sara refreshes -> 200, her new token now says manager
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh

> {%
  client.global.set('userToken', response.body.accessToken)
%}

### U48. Sara (manager) lists users -> 403 (the user list is admin only)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### U49. Sara (manager) tries to change a role -> 403
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "admin" }

### U50. Admin lists users -> 200, every account, with its role (admin and manager included)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### U51. Admin sets Sara back to user -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "user" }

### U52. Sara refreshes again so her token says user -> 200
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh

> {%
  client.global.set('userToken', response.body.accessToken)
%}

###
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE OWNER (U53 onwards)
# One-time step BEFORE U53: in Atlas, open the users collection, edit the document of
# the admin and add the field  isOwner  (type Boolean) with the value  true.
# New accounts are never owners. Run A and B in auth.http first, so adminToken and userToken are fresh
# and the cookie jar holds Sara's cookie (U60 and U70 need it).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### U53. The owner reads their own account -> 200, isOwner true
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### U54. Sara reads her own account -> 200, isOwner false
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### U55. Register with "isOwner": true and "role": "admin" in the body -> 201 the first time, 409 if she already exists (both are fine). The answer must say role user, isOwner false
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mallory",
  "email": "mallory@example.com",
  "password": "secret123",
  "isOwner": true,
  "role": "admin"
}

### U56. Sara changes her name and also sends "isOwner": true -> 200, isOwner stays false
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sara Ali", "isOwner": true }

### U57. Register Omar, a third account used as the target in the next tests -> 201 the first time, 409 if he already exists (both are fine)
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Omar Hassan",
  "email": "omar@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### U58. Login as Omar -> 200, saves omarId
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "omar@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

> {%
  client.global.set('omarId', response.body.user.id)
%}

### U59. The owner makes Sara an admin -> 200, role admin, isOwner false
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "admin" }

### U60. Sara refreshes -> 200, her new token now says admin
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh

> {%
  client.global.set('userToken', response.body.accessToken)
%}

### U61. Sara (admin, but not the owner) tries to change the owner -> 403 "Nobody can change the owner's role"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{adminId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "user" }

### U62. Sara tries to make Omar an admin -> 403 "Only the owner can make or remove admins"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{omarId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "admin" }

### U63. Sara makes Omar a manager -> 200 (admins can still move people between user and manager)
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{omarId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "manager" }

### U64. Sara sets Omar back to user -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{omarId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "user" }

### U65. The owner makes Omar an admin -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{omarId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "admin" }

### U66. Sara tries to demote Omar (now an admin) -> 403 "Only the owner can make or remove admins"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{omarId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "user" }

### U67. The owner demotes Omar back to user -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{omarId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "user" }

### U68. The owner takes Sara's admin rights away -> 200, role user (Sara's token still says admin for now)
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "user" }

### U69. Sara uses her OLD admin token -> 403 "You are not allowed to access this route" (the database says she is not an admin any more)
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{omarId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "manager" }

### U70. Sara refreshes -> 200, her token says user again
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh

> {%
  client.global.set('userToken', response.body.accessToken)
%}

### U71. The owner lists users -> 200, exactly one account has isOwner true
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}